    "updated_at": "2016-01-30T21:11:47Z",
    "body": "I tend to like the idea of a clean source file a bit more, but I don't feel strongly. Could you outline the concrete gain we're hoping for here? Is it just that maintaining the bibliography against redirects, dead links, http -> https transitions, and the like is a burden? @annevk mentioned typos upthread, but I don't quite see how pruning the bibliography helps.\n",
