    "created_at": "2016-01-31T00:28:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-31T00:28:40Z",
    "body": "I don’t feel strongly either but I think it’s preferable to not leave cruft around in the source that’s no longer serving any purpose—and, going forward, to have the ability to remove the cruft before ti (re)accumulates.\n\nWhat I mean is: It’s useful for us and contributors to know when a PR causes a reference to no longer be needed. That seems like the most appropriate point at which any unused references should get removed. But without these changes we have no way to alert contributors that as part of a PR they make, they should also remove any reference it causes to become unused that’d otherwise be left hanging around.\n\nSo to me the https://github.com/whatwg/wattsi/pull/17 change that goes along with this is adding useful functionality which would be helpful for both contributors and us to have.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
