    "created_at": "2016-01-31T10:21:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-31T10:21:42Z",
    "body": "> Could you outline the concrete gain we're hoping for here? Is it just that maintaining the bibliography against redirects, dead links, http -> https transitions, and the like is a burden?\n\nI stumbled upon it when looking for \"http://dev.w3.org/\" when updating the WebVTT reference, and asking \"do these need to be updated, have they moved to GitHub?\" only to find they were dangling. It's a very small nuisance, but it's similar to why I don't like leaving unused classes or functions in source code \"just in case,\" as occasionally you ask what it's there for and come up empty.\n\nI think what @sideshowbarker says about noticing when something becomes unused is a stronger argument, as it _could_ catch cases where we remove some spec text including a ref, but that reference is actually still needed, and should be added somewhere close by instead.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
